  "reasoning": "The facts show the defendant used violence, threats, and detention of ID cards to force victims to work for him, paying only minimal wages. This constitutes illegal detention (非法拘禁) and the crime of organizing/forcing others into slave labor (which is covered under illegal detention/forced labor statutes). He also assaulted victims, causing at least light injuries, which is intentional injury (故意伤害). The death of one victim resulted from the assault, but the prosecution emphasizes intentional injury and the resulting death, so the primary applicable charge is intentional injury (including the death consequence). No evidence of contract fraud, credit card fraud, or bill fraud is present, so those companion charges are not included.",
  "final_answer": "[故意伤害;非法拘禁]"
}

